+| Type           | Description                                          | Historical resolution priority           |
+| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
+| `BUNDLE`       | Worker bundle (application code)                     | From bundle: Bundle → Builtin → Fallback |
+| `HOST_PRIVATE` | Opt-in host entrypoint/prelude namespace             | Not used without module policy           |
+| `BUILTIN`      | Runtime modules (`node:*`, `cloudflare:*`)           | From builtin: Builtin → Internal         |
+| `INTERNAL`     | Only importable by builtins (`node-internal:*`)      | From internal: Internal only             |
+
+An opt-in closed module policy changes application-facing resolution in both
+module implementations. `BUNDLE` can resolve only declared `BUNDLE` definitions;
+`HOST_PRIVATE` can resolve declared host-private definitions plus the exact
+configured application main. Direct host entrypoint resolution is a distinct
+context, so application and host definitions with the same logical name retain
+separate identities. Unattributed and generated eval/Function scripts default to
+application provenance. Builtin and fallback behavior is unchanged when the
+policy is absent.
 
